WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
A Catholic school runs
a food bank collection.

2
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:06.100
Tins and packets pile up by the door.

3
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.600
Jesus told of a Samaritan who stopped
on the road to help a stranger.

4
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.150
His closing words: go and do likewise.

5
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:20.000
In 1891, Pope Leo the Thirteenth wrote a
whole letter about the lives of workers.

6
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:25.780
So is giving to charity enough, or do
Catholics believe God asks for more?

7
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:30.010
In this mission, you'll explore key
principles of Catholic Social Teaching,

8
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.260
from solidarity to peace.

9
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:38.260
Then you'll weigh up a hard claim: that
changing society is not the Church's job.

10
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.310
Your mission: find out
whether charity is enough,

11
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.200
or whether Catholics
believe God asks for more.
